Adaptation: Go per-position speculative acceptance accounting. The enginestep
per-position verified/accepted counters, the fixed slot cap whose last slot
aggregates deeper drafts, and the test-only mean |accept_prob - confidence|
over verify rows adapt the upstream sampler and stats logger. Upstream
telemetry reports the marginal accepted/verified rate per position; the
censored conditional rate (accepted/reached, where reached means every earlier
draft in the round was accepted) is a Fak-native estimator inspired by the
per-token conditional confidence semantics in scheduler.hpp, added beside the
unchanged marginal rate in internal/polymodel and as a reached counter in
internal/enginestep. The test oracle computes acceptance as the exact
sum_x min(target_x, draft_x) with no DRAFT_PROB_PENALTY, where upstream uses
max(1 - sum relu(target - penalized draft), 0). No upstream code is copied.
